{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++17 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++17 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nThis is an easier version of the problem. In this version, $$$n \\le 6$$$.Marek is working hard on creating strong testcases to his new algorithmic problem. You want to know what it is? Nah, we're not telling you. However, we can tell you how he generates the testcases.Marek chooses an integer $$$n$$$ and $$$n^2$$$ integers $$$p_{ij}$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$, $$$1 \\le j \\le n$$$). He then generates a random bipartite graph with $$$2n$$$ vertices. There are $$$n$$$ vertices on the left side: $$$\\ell_1, \\ell_2, \\dots, \\ell_n$$$, and $$$n$$$ vertices on the right side: $$$r_1, r_2, \\dots, r_n$$$. For each $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$, he puts an edge between vertices $$$\\ell_i$$$ and $$$r_j$$$ with probability $$$p_{ij}$$$ percent.It turns out that the tests will be strong only if a perfect matching exists in the generated graph. What is the probability that this will occur?It can be shown that this value can be represented as $$$\\frac{P}{Q}$$$ where $$$P$$$ and $$$Q$$$ are coprime integers and $$$Q \\not\\equiv 0 \\pmod{10^9+7}$$$. Let $$$Q^{-1}$$$ be an integer for which $$$Q \\cdot Q^{-1} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{10^9+7}$$$. Print the value of $$$P \\cdot Q^{-1}$$$ modulo $$$10^9+7$$$.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++17 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n#include <Modular.h>\n\nusing modular = Modular<1000000007>;\n\nint main() {\n    std::ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    std::cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    int n;\n    std::cin >> n;\n    \n    std::vector<modular> prob(n * n);\n    for (auto& p : prob) {\n        int x;\n        std::cin >> x;\n        p = modular(x) / 100;\n    }\n\n    std::vector<modular> dp(1 << n);\n    int half = n / 2;\n\n    auto computeMask = [&]() {\n        std::array<int, 64> mask;\n        int cnt = 0;\n        for (int m = 0; m < (1 << 6); ++m) {\n            mask[m] = (__builtin_popcount(m) == half) ? cnt++ : -1;\n        }\n        dp.resize(1 << cnt);\n        return mask;\n    };\n    auto maskVal = computeMask();\n\n    auto process = [&](int l, int r, auto&& f) {\n        int len = r - l;\n        for (int edgeMask = 0; edgeMask < (1 << (len * n)); ++edgeMask) {\n            modular p = 1;\n            for (int i = l * n, tmp = edgeMask; i < r * n; ++i, tmp >>= 1) {\n                p *= (tmp & 1) ? prob[i] : (1 - prob[i]);\n                if (p == 0) goto nextEdge;\n            }\n\n            std::array<int, 6> arr{};\n            int matchSets = 0;\n            while (true) {\n                int msk = 0;\n                bool ok = true;\n                for (int i = 0; i < len; ++i) {\n                    if (!(edgeMask >> (i * n + arr[i]) & 1)) { ok = false; break; }\n                    if (msk & (1 << arr[i])) { ok = false; break; }\n                    msk |= 1 << arr[i];\n                }\n                if (!ok) goto nextArr;\n                if (r == n) msk ^= (1 << n) - 1;\n                int idx = maskVal[msk];\n                if (idx != -1) matchSets |= 1 << idx;\n\nnextArr:\n                int i = len - 1;\n                while (i >= 0 && arr[i] == n - 1) {\n                    arr[i] = 0;\n                    --i;\n                }\n                if (i < 0) break;\n                ++arr[i];\n            }\n\n            f(matchSets, p);\nnextEdge:;\n        }\n    };\n\n    process(0, half, [&](int s, modular val) { dp[s] += val; });\n    for (int d = 1; d < (int)dp.size(); d <<= 1) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < (int)dp.size(); ++i) {\n            if (!(i & d)) dp[i | d] += dp[i];\n        }\n    }\n\n    modular ans{};\n    process(half, n, [&](int s, modular val) {\n        ans += val * (dp.back() - dp[(1 << n) - 1 - s]);\n    });\n    std::cout << (int)ans << '\\n';\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing modular = long long;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nmodular modPow(modular base, long long exp) {\n    modular result = 1;\n    base %= MOD;\n    while (exp > 0) {\n        if (exp & 1) result = (result * base) % MOD;\n        base = (base * base) % MOD;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nmodular modInverse(modular a) {\n    return modPow(a, MOD - 2);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    std::ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    std::cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    int n;\n    std::cin >> n;\n    \n    vector<vector<modular>> prob(n, vector<modular>(n));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n            int x;\n            std::cin >> x;\n            prob[i][j] = (modular)x * modInverse(100) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // dp[mask] = probability that we can match left vertices in mask to some right vertices\n    vector<modular> dp(1 << n, 0);\n    dp[0] = 1;\n\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << n); mask++) {\n        int cnt = __builtin_popcount(mask);\n        if (cnt == n) continue;\n        \n        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n            if (mask & (1 << j)) continue;\n            \n            modular p = 1;\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                if (mask & (1 << i)) continue;\n                p = p * (1 - prob[i][j] + MOD) % MOD;\n            }\n            \n            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                if (mask & (1 << i)) continue;\n                modular newP = dp[mask] * prob[i][j] % MOD;\n                dp[mask | (1 << j)] = (dp[mask | (1 << j)] + newP) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Use inclusion-exclusion to compute probability of perfect matching\n    vector<modular> f(1 << n, 0);\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << n); mask++) {\n        f[mask] = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if (mask & (1 << i)) {\n                for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n                    if (mask & (1 << j)) {\n                        f[mask] = f[mask] * prob[i][j] % MOD;\n                    } else {\n                        f[mask] = f[mask] * (1 - prob[i][j] + MOD) % MOD;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    vector<modular> g(1 << n, 0);\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << n); mask++) {\n        g[mask] = f[mask];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if (mask & (1 << i)) {\n                g[mask] = (g[mask] - g[mask ^ (1 << i)] + MOD) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    modular ans = g[(1 << n) - 1];\n    cout << ans << '\\n';\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.3\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-4.768370445162873e-07, -7.30726242181845e-05, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.3708974620385561e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576214658096433e-05, -3.564294092939235e-05, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -5.722029527532868e-06, -0.4740821123123169, -2.288792165927589e-05, -0.16146014630794525, -3.325883881188929e-05, -0.0002965487365145236, -0.11839034408330917, -0.23166655004024506, -2.753696753643453e-05, -0.0035277295392006636, -2.5033637939486653e-05, -0